{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"The expression for $g(x)$ includes an exponential term.\n\nRemember that the derivative of the general exponential term $a^x$ (where $a$ is any positive constant) is $\\ln(a)\\cdot a^x$.\n\nPut another way, $\\dfrac{d}{dx}(a^x)=\\ln(a)\\cdot a^x$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"$\\begin{align}\ng'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(-4\\cdot3^x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-4\\dfrac{d}{dx}(3^x)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-4\\cdot\\ln(3)\\cdot3^x\n\\\\\\\\\n\\end{align}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"In conclusion, $g'(x)=-4\\ln(3)\\cdot3^x$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $g(x)=-4\\cdot3^x$.\n\n**Find $g'(x)$.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]\n\n","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$-4\\ln(3)\\cdot 3^x$","correct":true},{"content":"$-4\\ln(x)\\cdot 3^x$","correct":false},{"content":"$-4\\log_3(x)\\cdot 3^x$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$-4\\cdot 3^{x-1}$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":true},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
